The VM base image (image/) is built on exeuntu by Bold Software, the image
of exe.dev, also under the Apache License 2.0:
https://github.com/boldsoftware/exeuntu
image/Dockerfile starts from a pinned exeuntu release and adds our layer:
image/boxe-init, image/boxe-welcome.sh, image/sshd-boxe.conf,
image/ssh-early.conf, image/boxe-sshkeys.service, image/boxe-rename-user.sh,
image/boxe-agents.service, and the changes made by the
RUN steps of image/Dockerfile (SSH as a plain service, no nologin, welcome
message, instructions for coding agents, the user renamed to boxedev).

cmd/boxeuntu, the image's tool for its coding agents, is a fork of exeuntu's
CLI (https://github.com/boldsoftware/exeuntu/tree/main/cli, commit c6635f5),
Apache License 2.0. cmd/boxeuntu/internal/agentupdate and
cmd/boxeuntu/internal/piupdate are exeuntu's, modified: updating OpenCode no
longer installs exe.dev's plugin and removes it if present. cmd/boxeuntu/main.go
and cmd/boxeuntu/internal/agentconfig are ours. The image no longer includes
exeuntu's CLI, its OpenCode and pi plugins, nor exe-setup.service.

The image also includes Shelley by Bold Software, under the Apache License
2.0, unmodified: https://github.com/boldsoftware/shelley
image/shelley-socket.conf and image/shelley-service.conf change how it is
started (port, no exe.dev gateway).

The image also includes exe-scroll by exe.dev, under the MIT License,
unmodified, from its release binaries:
https://github.com/boldsoftware/exe.dev/tree/main/exe-scroll
Its license is in image/exe-scroll-LICENSE, and in the image at
/usr/share/doc/exe-scroll/LICENSE. image/scroll is ours.

The image also installs KasmVNC by Kasm Technologies, under the GNU General
Public License 2.0, unmodified, from its release packages:
https://github.com/kasmtech/KasmVNC
The image does not include the KasmVNC source code: whoever distributes a
built image must also offer the corresponding source of that KasmVNC release,
as the GPL requires.

The Laravel image (image/laravel/) adds Composer (MIT) and Node.js (MIT and
others, license kept in /usr/share/licenses/nodejs/LICENSE), unmodified, from
their official releases.

boxe runs VMs with Cloud Hypervisor (Apache License 2.0 and BSD 3-Clause),
https://github.com/cloud-hypervisor/cloud-hypervisor, and a Linux kernel built
from https://github.com/cloud-hypervisor/linux (GNU General Public License
2.0) with kernel/config-7.2.8-boxe. Neither is included in this repository:
they are installed separately, as the README explains.

The website (site/) uses the fonts Archivo and JetBrains Mono, under the SIL
Open Font License 1.1 (site/fonts/OFL-Archivo.txt,
site/fonts/OFL-JetBrainsMono.txt).

boxed serves ghostty-web by Coder, under the MIT License, for the web
terminal: https://github.com/coder/ghostty-web (release 0.4.0). The files are
in cmd/boxed/term/ with its license (ghostty-web-LICENSE); ghostty-web.js is
modified only to drop the copy of the WebAssembly module it inlines, which
boxed serves as ghostty-vt.wasm instead.
